# Keeps the Docker build context, and with it the image (the runtime stage
# does `COPY . .`), free of local secrets and dev-only files. Without this
# file an image built from a working folder carries a real .env (which the
# app then reads from /app/.env), data/api_keys.json, .git, .venv and
# .claude/ in its layers (CWE-538).
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern here matches only at the context root;
# use **/ for any depth. The last matching line wins, so a `!` exception has
# to come after the exclusion it undoes. tests/test_dockerignore.py pins both
# directions: secrets stay out, and no tracked file the image needs is dropped.

# Secrets and local state. Docker Compose passes .env at run time (env_file)
# and mounts ./data as a volume, so neither has to be in the image. Compose
# override files are local by design and often carry secrets too.
.env*
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
docker-compose.override.y*ml
compose.override.y*ml

# Version control, CI, editors, AI assistants
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
.clone
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.vscode
.idea

# Python environments, caches, build output, OS clutter
.venv
venv
env
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
*.egg-info
build
dist
.tools
ffmpeg
tmp
**/*.tmp
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Local-only notes and screenshots (gitignored, so never in a clean checkout)
docs-internal
docs/*.png
docs/*.jpg
docs/*.jpeg
CLAUDE.md
*-this-session-is-being-continued-*.txt

# Not needed at run time
tests
